-- bloom-filters (npm), CuckooFilter.create(n, errorRate): the fingerprint keeps about half the bits that
-- the error-rate formula asks for, so the false positive rate is far above errorRate.
--
-- What the code does. Line numbers are for master at e2882ef (src/) and for the published 3.0.4 build
-- (dist/, the same code as tag v3.0.4); the logic below is the same in both.
--
--   computeFingerpintLength  src/cuckoo/cuckoo-filter.ts:25-36    dist/cuckoo/cuckoo-filter.js:57-68
--     f = ceil(log2(1/rate) + log2(2 * bucketSize)) bits, then returns ceil(f / 8), documented as
--     "the optimal fingerprint length in bytes". Up to 1.3.9 it returned ceil(f / 4), "because we use
--     base 16 64-bits hashes"; 2.0.0 changed it to ceil(f / 8).
--   create                   src/cuckoo/cuckoo-filter.ts:87-96    dist/cuckoo/cuckoo-filter.js:107-113
--     bucketSize defaults to 4; the fingerprint length is computeFingerpintLength(bucketSize, errorRate).
--   _locations               src/cuckoo/cuckoo-filter.ts:319-339  dist/cuckoo/cuckoo-filter.js:329-345
--     fingerprint = hashes.string.substring(0, fingerprintLength), where hashes.string is the hash in
--     hexadecimal: src/hashing.ts:163-166 (hash.toString(16)); dist/hashing/hashing.js:208-211 and
--     dist/utils.js:65-71 (numberToHex). A character holds 4 bits, not 8.
--   has                      src/cuckoo/cuckoo-filter.ts:280-286  dist/cuckoo/cuckoo-filter.js:295-299
--     true if bucket firstIndex or bucket secondIndex holds the query's fingerprint.
--   rate                     src/cuckoo/cuckoo-filter.ts:292-296  dist/cuckoo/cuckoo-filter.js:304-308
--     2^(log2(2 * bucketSize) - load * (fingerprintLength / load)) = 2 * bucketSize / 2^fingerprintLength.
--
-- Abstraction. Haze has no log2, so the model uses errorRate = 1/1024, for which the formula gives exactly
-- f = 13 (checked below); errorRate 0.001 gives 13 too. Fingerprints are independent and uniform over
-- 2^(4 * length) values. 3.0.4 pads the 32-bit hash to 8 hex characters, so this holds there except for
-- hashes below 2^16; master doesn't pad, so its first character is never '0' and its real rate is a
-- little higher than the model's. A query meets 2 * bucketSize stored fingerprints, as with two full
-- buckets, which is the case the formula's bound 2 * bucketSize / 2^f is for. At the load create() gives
-- (0.954 for n items) a query meets 7.6 on average, and the shipped rate is above errorRate once the
-- filter is more than about 3% full. Bucket indexes are left out: they decide which stored fingerprints a
-- query meets, not how likely each one is to match. The fix counts the length in hex characters again,
-- ceil(f / 4), and rate() uses 4 bits per character.

def b : Num := 4                     -- create()'s default bucketSize
def error_rate : Num := 1/1024
def f_bits : Num := 13               -- ceil(log2(1024) + log2(2 * 4))

def pow2(k : Num) : Num := if k <= 0 then 1 else 2 * pow2(k - 1)
def ceil(x : Num) : Num := 0 - floor(0 - x)

-- f is the smallest number of bits with 2b / 2^f <= errorRate, which is what the formula computes.
theorem f_matches_formula : 2 * b / pow2(f_bits) <= error_rate and 2 * b / pow2(f_bits - 1) > error_rate

-- 1. The mechanism: computeFingerpintLength returns ceil(f / 8), and _locations keeps that many hex
--    characters. For bucketSize 4, f runs from 8 (errorRate 0.04, the README example) to 63 (1e-18, the
--    README's limit).
def chars_shipped(f : Num) : Num := ceil(f / 8)
def chars_fixed(f : Num) : Num := ceil(f / 4)

theorem shipped_keeps_f_bits : forall f in 8..63, 4 * chars_shipped(f) >= f
theorem fixed_keeps_f_bits : forall f in 8..63, 4 * chars_fixed(f) >= f

-- 2. The promise: create(n, errorRate) is "optimal for a number of items and a desired error rate"
--    (README), errorRate being "the error rate, i.e. 'false positive' rate, targetted by the filter"
--    (computeFingerpintLength). A query that was never added is a false positive when one of the 2b
--    stored fingerprints it meets equals its own. With fingerprints uniform over V values, the number
--    that do is binomial(2b, 1/V).
input matches_shipped : Num ~ binomial(2 * b, 1 / pow2(4 * chars_shipped(f_bits)))   -- 2 chars, 8 bits
input matches_fixed : Num ~ binomial(2 * b, 1 / pow2(4 * chars_fixed(f_bits)))       -- 4 chars, 16 bits

claim shipped_meets_error_rate : matches_shipped >= 1 with prob <= 1/1024             -- errorRate
claim fixed_meets_error_rate : matches_fixed >= 1 with prob <= 1/1024

-- 3. rate(): "compute the filter's false positive rate (or error rate)" (README). When it was added, as
--    fpr in #9, it "should be less than the desired error_rate you previously defined using the create
--    method". It counts each character as one bit.
def rate_shipped : Num := 2 * b / pow2(chars_shipped(f_bits))
def rate_fixed : Num := 2 * b / pow2(4 * chars_fixed(f_bits))

#eval rate_shipped
theorem shipped_rate_within_error_rate : rate_shipped <= error_rate
theorem fixed_rate_within_error_rate : rate_fixed <= error_rate
